	quest.544D301000100001.title: "Welcome to Too Much Magic"
	quest.544D301000100001.quest_desc: ["A magic-first modpack with many independent schools. Introduction gives you the essentials, Progression connects systems, and the other groups guide individual mods. Check this entry when you have read it."]
	quest.544D4D1100000001.title: "Punch a Tree"
	quest.544D4D1100000001.quest_desc: ["Pick up any log or stem to receive one 27-slot Trinkets Pouch automatically per player. Claim this quest's experience and torches separately. Do not place portable bags inside other bags; cross-mod enforcement is still in development."]
	quest.544D501000300000.title: "Make a Crafting Table"
	quest.544D501000300000.quest_desc: ["Craft a table to unlock the familiar 3x3 crafting grid. It is a useful baseline before you explore magical crafting."]
	quest.544D501001300000.title: "Choose Your First Path"
	quest.544D501001300000.quest_desc: ["Choose one starter gift for a path you want to try: Ars Nouveau, Iron's Spells, fishing, Botania, Occultism or exploration. This one-time personal reward does not lock a class. You may pursue every other magic mod later. An empty spellbook may still need spells or scrolls before you can cast."]
	quest.544D501000400000.title: "Make a Wooden Pickaxe"
	quest.544D501000400000.quest_desc: ["Craft your first wooden pickaxe. Ordinary tools are an easy way to get established before specializing in magic."]
	quest.544D501000500000.title: "Gather Stone"
	quest.544D501000500000.quest_desc: ["Collect sixteen cobblestone. Stone is useful for your first shelter, tools and furnace."]
	quest.544D501000600000.title: "Upgrade to Stone"
	quest.544D501000600000.quest_desc: ["Make a stone pickaxe so you can mine sturdier resources."]
	quest.544D501000700000.title: "A Place for Your Things"
	quest.544D501000700000.quest_desc: ["Craft a chest for early base storage. Magic eventually offers more specialized options than generic storage networks."]
	quest.544D501000800000.title: "Light the Furnace"
	quest.544D501000800000.quest_desc: ["Craft a furnace. Smelting remains useful alongside later magical processing."]
	quest.544D501000900000.title: "Find Your First Iron"
	quest.544D501000900000.quest_desc: ["Bring back three raw iron. Magical mining and transmutation will eventually provide alternatives."]
	quest.544D501000A00000.title: "Iron Pickaxe"
	quest.544D501000A00000.quest_desc: ["Craft an iron pickaxe. You now have the baseline tools to choose your first magical specialty."]
	quest.544D501000B00000.title: "Begin a Library"
	quest.544D501000B00000.quest_desc: ["Craft a book to begin collecting magical research and manuals. Akashic Tome can organize compatible guides without replacing each school's progression."]
	quest.544D501000C00000.title: "Build a Bookshelf"
	quest.544D501000C00000.quest_desc: ["Craft a bookshelf to establish a magical research corner. Bookshelves also appear in early Scriptor Magicae tools. The spellbook and world-specific magical vocabulary must still be acquired or discovered."]
	quest.544D501000D00000.title: "Prepare a Field Kit"
	quest.544D501000D00000.quest_desc: ["Make a barrel for sorting the ingredients, tools and supplies you carry between your first magical projects. This is a practical storage milestone, not a requirement to specialize in any particular school."]
	quest.544D501000E00000.title: "Build a Research Lectern"
	quest.544D501000E00000.quest_desc: ["Craft a lectern for your early magical library. This is the ordinary Minecraft lectern; Scriptor Magicae has a separate Casting Lectern for fuel-free smelting. Check JEI before confusing the two."]
	quest.544D501000F00000.title: "Try a First Spell or Ritual"
	quest.544D501000F00000.quest_desc: ["Use any school's introductory magic: cast an Ars spell, perform a first Occultism ritual, make use of EvilCraft blood, try witchcraft, or write a Scriptor spell. This checkmark is manual because there is no honest single automatic criterion shared by all schools."]
	quest.544D501001000000.title: "A Little Protection"
	quest.544D501001000000.quest_desc: ["Craft an iron chestplate for dangerous exploring. This is optional: players who prefer farming, research or base magic can progress without rushing combat."]
	quest.544D501001100000.title: "Scout with a Spyglass"
	quest.544D501001100000.quest_desc: ["Use copper and amethyst to build a spyglass for scouting structures and terrain. This is an optional exploration aid; you can still prefer base magic, rituals or farming."]
	quest.544D501001200000.title: "Chart Your Next Journey"
	quest.544D501001200000.quest_desc: ["Use an empty map to create a filled map of your next destination. The quest book provides independent paths through every magic school; this optional task concludes onboarding without locking your choices."]
	quest.544D301000200001.title: "Tips \\& Tricks Index"
	quest.544D301000200001.quest_desc: ["These optional read-and-check tips cover tools, keys and systems that a large modpack makes easy to overlook. The tips are not compulsory progression gates."]
	quest.544D502000200000.title: "Find Recipes with JEI"
	quest.544D502000200000.quest_desc: ["Use Just Enough Items to explore recipes and item usages. Check both directions before assuming a resource has only one way to obtain it."]
	quest.544D502000300000.title: "Identify Blocks with Jade"
	quest.544D502000300000.quest_desc: ["Jade identifies blocks and creatures under your crosshair and can display useful supported-mod information."]
	quest.544D502000400000.title: "Sort Your Inventory"
	quest.544D502000400000.quest_desc: ["Inventory Tweaks ReFoxed provides inventory sorting and refill features. Middle-click sorting depends on key bindings and the container; Mouse Tweaks also changes dragging and scrolling."]
	quest.544D502000500000.title: "Use Crafting Tweaks"
	quest.544D502000500000.quest_desc: ["Crafting Tweaks can rotate, balance or clear a normal crafting grid. Test those controls before assuming they work in a modded ritual interface."]
	quest.544D502000600000.title: "Search the Controls Screen"
	quest.544D502000600000.quest_desc: ["Use the controls search to find conflicting mod keys. KeyBind Bundles can help organize different play styles."]
	quest.544D502000700000.title: "Gather Your Guidebooks"
	quest.544D502000700000.quest_desc: ["Akashic Tome can collect compatible magic manuals into one book. Not every guide is compatible and you may need to acquire some books individually."]
	quest.544D502000800000.title: "Curios and Portable Bags"
	quest.544D502000800000.quest_desc: ["Curios provides extra equipment slots. Never nest portable bags: Ars Elemental has a partial blacklist, but Occultism and ProjectE require more complete safeguards before survival release."]
	quest.544D502000900000.title: "Claim Your Base"
	quest.544D502000900000.quest_desc: ["Use FTB Chunks to claim an area around your base. Chunk loading depends on server settings; protection and backups solve different problems."]
	quest.544D502000A00000.title: "Understand Lootr Chests"
	quest.544D502000A00000.quest_desc: ["Lootr supports per-player loot in many generated chests. Exact behavior can depend on the structure and container."]
	quest.544D502000B00000.title: "Plan for Death"
	quest.544D502000B00000.quest_desc: ["Corail Tombstone changes recovery after death. Learn how graves work before a dangerous expedition, and keep backups while death-handler compatibility is under review."]
	quest.544D502000C00000.title: "Search Biomes"
	quest.544D502000C00000.quest_desc: ["Nature's Compass can locate biomes relevant to exploration and magic. It is not a Waystone or teleport system."]
	quest.544D502000D00000.title: "Resolve Recipe Conflicts"
	quest.544D502000D00000.quest_desc: ["Polymorph can help when multiple recipes have the same ingredients. Check the intended output before spending scarce materials."]
	quest.544D502000E00000.title: "Understand Character Growth"
	quest.544D502000E00000.quest_desc: ["Pufferfish's Skills and Attributes will support the custom skill tree; Improvable Skills is separate. The two do not share a unified point pool."]
	quest.544D502000F00000.title: "Zoom and Overlay Controls"
	quest.544D502000F00000.quest_desc: ["Just Zoom and More Overlays Updated offer visual aids. Adjust key bindings if they conflict with other mod controls."]
	quest.544D502001000000.title: "Use the Quest Shop"
	quest.544D502001000000.quest_desc: ["Use /hqs shop to browse a curated list of convenience supplies, common magical materials, exploration finds, and specific Artifacts. Quest Shop coins belong to your FTB Team. Ordinary quests generally give thematic item rewards; specialized resource-selling quests pay coins."]
	quest.544D502001100000.title: "Smelt Without Fuel: Scriptor Lectern"
	quest.544D502001100000.quest_desc: ["Scriptor Magicae's Casting Lectern (scriptor:casting_lectern) casts a written Inflame spell automatically. Upstream recipe: three wooden slabs, one bookshelf, purple wool. Inflame consumes smeltable ingredients and creates normal furnace outputs without coal, FE or player mana. Total spell cost limits cadence and complexity (default maximum 25) rather than consuming a resource. You must learn this world's magic vocabulary and prepare a book. Our pinned 2.0.14 build still needs an actual adjacent-chest input/output test; do not promise fully unattended chest smelting until verified."]
	quest.544D502001200000.title: "Double Raw Ore: Occultism or Mahou?"
	quest.544D502001200000.quest_desc: ["Occultism's early Foliot Crusher turns supported raw ores into two dusts after its first spirit ritual; confirm that these dusts smelt in our pack. Mahou Tsukai's Mortar and Pestle presently produces two catalyst powders from ingots/gems, NOT two smeltable ingots from one raw ore. Our planned ore/dust unification is separate unfinished compatibility work. The cursed EvilCraft Vengeance Pickaxe boosts mined drops through Fortune instead of doubling furnace input."]
	quest.544D502001300000.title: "Need Early Flight? Compare Brooms"
	quest.544D502001300000.quest_desc: ["EvilCraft has a modular blood-powered broom. Hexerei has a different witch's broom. Both offer mobility before finding an Elytra, but have distinct recipes, fuels and handling. Check JEI and the appropriate Magic chapter; don't assume unlimited fuel or identical controls."]
	quest.544D502001400000.title: "Vengeance Pickaxe: Fortune with a Price"
	quest.544D502001400000.quest_desc: ["EvilCraft's Vengeance Pickaxe provides unusually high Fortune (often Fortune V) with a dangerous Vengeance curse. Upstream crafting uses diamonds, hardened blood and undead wood. It increases drops from ore mining; it does not automatically smelt ore or mine entire veins. Learn the curse before using it on dangerous expeditions."]
	quest.544D301000300001.title: "Food \\& Fishing Index"
	quest.544D301000300001.quest_desc: ["Farming, fishing and cooking offer useful alternatives to combat foraging. Explore these branches independently and use JEI for the many additional Pam's HarvestCraft recipes."]
	quest.544D503000200000.title: "Start with Seeds"
	quest.544D503000200000.quest_desc: ["Collect wheat seeds to start a farm. The installed food mods offer many additional crops as you explore."]
	quest.544D503000300000.title: "Prepare a Field"
	quest.544D503000300000.quest_desc: ["Craft a stone hoe to till farmland. Harvest with Ease can make managing mature crops simpler."]
	quest.544D503000400000.title: "Bring in the Wheat"
	quest.544D503000400000.quest_desc: ["Harvest four wheat. Ordinary grains form a foundation for many more elaborate meals."]
	quest.544D503000500000.title: "A Patch of Sugar Cane"
	quest.544D503000500000.quest_desc: ["Collect three sugar cane. Sugar and paper support cooking and magic books."]
	quest.544D503000600000.title: "Raise a Chicken Dinner"
	quest.544D503000600000.quest_desc: ["Acquire raw chicken. Farmer's Delight and Pam's HarvestCraft offer cooking options beyond simple smelting."]
	quest.544D503000700000.title: "Gather Eggs"
	quest.544D503000700000.quest_desc: ["Collect two eggs for cooking recipes."]
	quest.544D503000800000.title: "Fresh Milk"
	quest.544D503000800000.quest_desc: ["Get a bucket of milk. Many recipes need useful basic farm products as well as exotic ingredients."]
	quest.544D503000900000.title: "Ready Your Fishing Rod"
	quest.544D503000900000.quest_desc: ["Craft a fishing rod and start exploring another renewable food route."]
	quest.544D503000A00000.title: "Catch a Cod"
	quest.544D503000A00000.quest_desc: ["Catch cod using a rod. A small fishing expedition can feed a player before a serious farm is built."]
	quest.544D503000B00000.title: "Catch a Salmon"
	quest.544D503000B00000.quest_desc: ["Catch salmon in suitable water. Aquaculture expands this side of the game."]
	quest.544D503000C00000.title: "Aquaculture: Iron Rod"
	quest.544D503000C00000.quest_desc: ["Craft Aquaculture 2's iron fishing rod. Use JEI for its current exact recipe."]
	quest.544D503000D00000.title: "Aquaculture: Gold Rod"
	quest.544D503000D00000.quest_desc: ["Progress to an Aquaculture gold fishing rod. This is a distinct milestone, not another copy of the iron-rod objective."]
	quest.544D503000E00000.title: "Aquaculture: Neptunium Rod"
	quest.544D503000E00000.quest_desc: ["Obtain the rare Neptunium fishing rod as an optional long-term goal rather than an early prerequisite."]
	quest.544D503000F00000.title: "Light a Campfire"
	quest.544D503000F00000.quest_desc: ["Craft a campfire to cook basic food on the road."]
	quest.544D503001000000.title: "Farmer's Delight: Cutting Board"
	quest.544D503001000000.quest_desc: ["Craft Farmer's Delight's cutting board to prepare ingredients outside the normal crafting grid."]
	quest.544D503001100000.title: "Farmer's Delight: Cooking Pot"
	quest.544D503001100000.quest_desc: ["Make a cooking pot and use it with heat and ingredients for more satisfying meals."]
	quest.544D503001200000.title: "Find the Seed Market"
	quest.544D503001200000.quest_desc: ["Craft Farming for Blockheads' Market for ordinary seed and sapling trades. Magical seed trades must be audited before survival release."]
	quest.544D503001300000.title: "Pam's HarvestCraft: Fried Chicken"
	quest.544D503001300000.quest_desc: ["Craft a finished Fried Chicken from Pam's HarvestCraft 2 Food Core. A useful optional cooking challenge."]
	quest.544D503001400000.title: "Pam's HarvestCraft: Starfruit"
	quest.544D503001400000.quest_desc: ["Obtain starfruit from Pam's HarvestCraft 2 Trees, showcasing specialty plants and orchard progression."]
	quest.544D503001500000.title: "Cooking for Blockheads: Cooking Table"
	quest.544D503001500000.quest_desc: ["Build the Cooking Table to discover dishes available from nearby kitchen ingredients. Cooking for Blockheads works alongside Farmer's Delight and Pam's HarvestCraft, expanding an organized base kitchen."]
	quest.544D503001600000.title: "Cooking for Blockheads: Oven"
	quest.544D503001600000.quest_desc: ["Build an Oven to expand the modular kitchen. Check recipes and heating behavior in JEI and test compatibility with food ingredients before automating the kitchen."]
	quest.544D302000100001.title: "Chapter Overview"
	quest.544D302000100001.quest_desc: ["An introduction to Basic Progression in Too Much Magic.", "This chapter's full questline is still being written. This optional overview does not unlock or gate any other chapter."]
	quest.544D504000100000.title: "Sell Copper I — First Trade"
	quest.544D504000100000.quest_desc: ["Submit 8 pieces of copper as a one-time sale. The exchange consumes the materials and credits your team's Quest Shop balance with one coin. Later tiers require larger deliveries."]
	quest.544D504000200000.title: "Sell Copper II — Regular Buyer"
	quest.544D504000200000.quest_desc: ["Submit 32 pieces of copper as a one-time sale. The exchange consumes the materials and credits your team's Quest Shop balance with one coin. Later tiers require larger deliveries."]
	quest.544D504000300000.title: "Sell Copper III — Packed Shipment"
	quest.544D504000300000.quest_desc: ["Submit 16 blocks of copper as a one-time sale. The exchange consumes the materials and credits your team's Quest Shop balance with one coin. Later tiers require larger deliveries."]
	quest.544D504000400000.title: "Sell Copper IV — Industrial Exchange"
	quest.544D504000400000.quest_desc: ["Repeatable bulk sale: submit 256 full copper blocks (4 stacks) for a single coin. The items must be consumed. After ProjectE unlocks, manufacturing large quantities for shop currency is an intended late-game option."]
	quest.544D504000500000.title: "Sell Emeralds I — First Trade"
	quest.544D504000500000.quest_desc: ["Submit 2 pieces of emeralds as a one-time sale. The exchange consumes the materials and credits your team's Quest Shop balance with one coin. Later tiers require larger deliveries."]
	quest.544D504000600000.title: "Sell Emeralds II — Regular Buyer"
	quest.544D504000600000.quest_desc: ["Submit 8 pieces of emeralds as a one-time sale. The exchange consumes the materials and credits your team's Quest Shop balance with one coin. Later tiers require larger deliveries."]
	quest.544D504000700000.title: "Sell Emeralds III — Packed Shipment"
	quest.544D504000700000.quest_desc: ["Submit 16 blocks of emeralds as a one-time sale. The exchange consumes the materials and credits your team's Quest Shop balance with one coin. Later tiers require larger deliveries."]
	quest.544D504000800000.title: "Sell Emeralds IV — Industrial Exchange"
	quest.544D504000800000.quest_desc: ["Repeatable bulk sale: submit 128 full emeralds blocks (2 stacks) for a single coin. The items must be consumed. After ProjectE unlocks, manufacturing large quantities for shop currency is an intended late-game option."]
	quest.544D504000900000.title: "Sell Diamonds I — First Trade"
	quest.544D504000900000.quest_desc: ["Submit 1 pieces of diamonds as a one-time sale. The exchange consumes the materials and credits your team's Quest Shop balance with one coin. Later tiers require larger deliveries."]
	quest.544D504000A00000.title: "Sell Diamonds II — Regular Buyer"
	quest.544D504000A00000.quest_desc: ["Submit 4 pieces of diamonds as a one-time sale. The exchange consumes the materials and credits your team's Quest Shop balance with one coin. Later tiers require larger deliveries."]
	quest.544D504000B00000.title: "Sell Diamonds III — Packed Shipment"
	quest.544D504000B00000.quest_desc: ["Submit 8 blocks of diamonds as a one-time sale. The exchange consumes the materials and credits your team's Quest Shop balance with one coin. Later tiers require larger deliveries."]
	quest.544D504000C00000.title: "Sell Diamonds IV — Industrial Exchange"
	quest.544D504000C00000.quest_desc: ["Repeatable bulk sale: submit 64 full diamonds blocks (1 stack) for a single coin. The items must be consumed. After ProjectE unlocks, manufacturing large quantities for shop currency is an intended late-game option."]
	quest.544D504000D00000.title: "Choose a Magical Tradition"
	quest.544D504000D00000.quest_desc: ["Pick one school of magic that interests you, then open its own chapter. Ars Nouveau, Occultism, Botania, Hex Casting, and the other traditions can be explored in parallel. This is a guide checkmark, not a mandatory choice or a gate on the other chapters."]
	quest.544D504000E00000.title: "Secure Some Copper"
	quest.544D504000E00000.quest_desc: ["Bring back eight raw copper. Copper supports the world's ordinary utility blocks as well as several magical crafts. The separate coin-exchange branch consumes processed copper; gathering raw ore here is a distinct objective."]
	quest.544D504000F00000.title: "Prospect for Gold"
	quest.544D504000F00000.quest_desc: ["Find four raw gold. Gold is useful for redstone infrastructure, enchantment-related crafting and many magical ingredients."]
	quest.544D504001000000.title: "Learn to Recognize Lapis"
	quest.544D504001000000.quest_desc: ["Bring eight lapis lazuli. It supports enchantment and an assortment of magical recipes; JEI shows the exact uses in this pack."]
	quest.544D504001100000.title: "Collect Amethyst"
	quest.544D504001100000.quest_desc: ["Collect eight amethyst shards, or buy them from Quest Shop if the geology refuses to cooperate. A purchased ingredient is an intentional anti-grind alternative, not a bypass of any late-game boss gate."]
	quest.544D504001200000.title: "Bring a Water Bucket"
	quest.544D504001200000.quest_desc: ["Keep water accessible for building, agriculture, and many magical structures. This milestone is separate from Food \\& Fishing's milk-bucket quest."]
	quest.544D504001300000.title: "Defend Yourself"
	quest.544D504001300000.quest_desc: ["Make a shield. Early defensive options make it easier to travel while discovering spells and supernatural equipment."]
	quest.544D504001400000.title: "Upgrade to Diamond Mining"
	quest.544D504001400000.quest_desc: ["Craft a diamond pickaxe when you are ready to move beyond iron. It is a practical exploration baseline, not a requirement to pursue all magic schools."]
	quest.544D504001500000.title: "Reach the Nether for Ingredients"
	quest.544D504001500000.quest_desc: ["Acquire a blaze rod in the Nether. The Nether is one of several routes toward stronger magical ingredients and more dangerous encounters; this objective does not duplicate a specialist chapter's spellcasting milestone."]
	quest.544D504001600000.title: "Gather Ender Pearls"
	quest.544D504001600000.quest_desc: ["Collect four ender pearls. They support teleportation, several magical recipes and preparation for eventual End exploration."]
	quest.544D302000200001.title: "Chapter Overview"
	quest.544D302000200001.quest_desc: ["An introduction to Advanced Progression in Too Much Magic.", "This chapter's full questline is still being written. This optional overview does not unlock or gate any other chapter."]
	quest.544D505000100000.title: "Map Out Your Infrastructure"
	quest.544D505000100000.quest_desc: ["A developed magical base benefits from a few focused work areas: enchanting and potions, ritual floors, stable item storage, and safe power machinery. Many schools are independent; there is no mandatory universal industrial network."]
	quest.544D505000200000.title: "Install an Enchanting Table"
	quest.544D505000200000.quest_desc: ["Craft an enchanting table, add bookshelves when convenient, and compare enchantments to spellcasting upgrades. Apotheosis has deeper enchantment mechanics in its own chapter."]
	quest.544D505000300000.title: "Bring an Anvil"
	quest.544D505000300000.quest_desc: ["Craft an anvil for conventional repairs, naming, and combining compatible enchantments. This supplements magical equipment rather than replacing its unique upgrades."]
	quest.544D505000400000.title: "Build a Brewing Stand"
	quest.544D505000400000.quest_desc: ["Craft a brewing stand and explore potion recipes. Potion and herb-based systems also have specialized paths in Witchcraft, Hexerei and other chapters."]
	quest.544D505000500000.title: "Build a Portal Reserve"
	quest.544D505000500000.quest_desc: ["Bring ten obsidian for a safe portal or important construction work. Consider well-lit, protected portal sites; dimensions remain separate exploration branches."]
	quest.544D505000600000.title: "Keep an Ender Chest"
	quest.544D505000600000.quest_desc: ["Craft an Ender Chest for vanilla portable access to a personal inventory. Occultism remains the pack's featured expandable magical storage path, and generic item logistics networks remain excluded."]
	quest.544D505000700000.title: "Recover Ancient Debris Products"
	quest.544D505000700000.quest_desc: ["Acquire one Netherite Scrap to introduce late-game conventional material upgrades. This does not unlock boss-gated draconium or Replication materials."]
	quest.544D505000800000.title: "Construct a Lodestone"
	quest.544D505000800000.quest_desc: ["Craft a lodestone and use it with a compass as a reliable base or remote-site landmark. The pack deliberately does not include Waystones."]
	quest.544D505000900000.title: "Understand Summoning Rituals"
	quest.544D505000900000.quest_desc: ["Summoning Rituals is a custom recipe framework: it does not bring a complete fixed questline of ritual recipes by default. Check JEI and the TMM recipe registry for any implemented pack-specific offerings. Do not assume speculative rituals work until authored and tested."]
	quest.544D505000A00000.title: "Prepare a Protected Ritual Chamber"
	quest.544D505000A00000.quest_desc: ["Reserve sufficient space for multiblocks, separate hazardous machinery, and keep vulnerable farms and storage away from explosive experiments. This is a planning checkmark, not an automated claim that a structure exists."]
	quest.544D302000300001.title: "Chapter Overview"
	quest.544D302000300001.quest_desc: ["An introduction to Endgame Roadmap in Too Much Magic.", "This chapter's full questline is still being written. This optional overview does not unlock or gate any other chapter."]
	quest.544D506000100000.title: "Roadmap: Read Before the Endgame"
	quest.544D506000100000.quest_desc: ["This is a reference page, not another boss checklist. The Endgame category owns the actual Draconic Evolution, ProjectE and Replication quests, while Cataclysm and Occultism own their own unique milestones. Mark this read when you understand the links."]
	quest.544D506000200000.title: "Roadmap: The End and Draconic Materials"
	quest.544D506000200000.quest_desc: ["The End is a major progression junction: dragon encounters, dangerous exploration and draconium resources. The precise uranium and draconic-dust generation restrictions are still under design; the questbook cannot enforce a pending ore-generation rule."]
	quest.544D506000300000.title: "Roadmap: Cataclysm Boss Resources"
	quest.544D506000300000.quest_desc: ["The Harbinger and Ignis are proposed sources for late Eldritch Ancient Miner requirements. Their exact rewards and material keys must be verified in the installed Cataclysm version; this page does not grant boss loot or mark either boss defeated."]
	quest.544D506000400000.title: "Roadmap: Occultism's Final Miner"
	quest.544D506000400000.quest_desc: ["The Eldritch Ancient Miner is intended to offer a difficult renewable Replication ore route. The proposed cost is two to four Marid-tier components plus high-level boss materials, possibly late Botania; none of these recipe changes is assumed implemented."]
	quest.544D506000500000.title: "Roadmap: Chaos Guardian as the Gate"
	quest.544D506000500000.quest_desc: ["Defeating the Chaos Guardian must precede every usable ProjectE and Project Expansion acquisition or function. This is a rule for actual gameplay enforcement, not something a checked roadmap page can unlock. The boss objective belongs to Draconic Evolution's Endgame chapter."]
	quest.544D506000600000.title: "Roadmap: What Unlocks Afterwards"
	quest.544D506000600000.quest_desc: ["After verified Chaos Guardian completion, pursue the ProjectE and Project Expansion progression, Gem Armor and other genuinely late options. Replication and its miner route remain a separate arc. Re:Avaritia, Extended Crafting and the Ring of the Seven Deadly Sins are excluded."]
	quest.544D302000400001.title: "Chapter Overview"
	quest.544D302000400001.quest_desc: ["An introduction to Skills \\& Advancement in Too Much Magic.", "This chapter's full questline is still being written. This optional overview does not unlock or gate any other chapter."]
	quest.544D507000100000.title: "Read the Two Skill Systems"
	quest.544D507000100000.quest_desc: ["This pack includes Pufferfish's Skills, Pufferfish's Attributes and Improvable Skills 3. The Pufferfish framework is meant to host TMM's custom cross-mod magic trees, but that tree is not published yet; do not assume unimplemented magic bonuses."]
	quest.544D507000200000.title: "Open the Skill Interface"
	quest.544D507000200000.quest_desc: ["Find Pufferfish's Skills in the controls/UI once the client is running. Inspect the interface and available trees. This is a manual learning checkmark, not a claim that the custom magic progression data is already available."]
	quest.544D507000300000.title: "Understand Attributes"
	quest.544D507000300000.quest_desc: ["Pufferfish's Attributes can expose and modify stats used by combat and magic systems. Before specialization, examine what each stat actually changes in this pack; do not assume cooldown, damage and resource effects apply to every mod."]
	quest.544D507000400000.title: "Experiment with Improvable Skills"
	quest.544D507000400000.quest_desc: ["Improvable Skills 3 is a separate experience-powered perk system. Spend points only when you know what an upgrade does. Do not assume its perks are the same as the custom Pufferfish magic tree."]
	quest.544D507000500000.title: "Inspect Cooldown and Casting Perks"
	quest.544D507000500000.quest_desc: ["The planned skill tree emphasizes cooldown, skill efficiency and relevant item-crafting boosts rather than adding new global mana bars. Individual spell systems differ; some have no meaningful Pufferfish hook and should not receive fake bonuses."]
	quest.544D507000600000.title: "Plan for Practical Attribute Caps"
	quest.544D507000600000.quest_desc: ["Some attributes have real mechanical limits (such as cooldown reduction). Others may eventually support very large values within their mods. Exact caps and any special bridging code belong to separate configuration work, not an undocumented quest reward."]
	quest.544D507000700000.title: "Choose How to Specialize"
	quest.544D507000700000.quest_desc: ["Advance whichever magical tradition interests you. Skill progress and individual spellbook or ritual progress are not necessarily shared; quests guide your choice without forcing every school down one main path."]
	quest.544D302000500001.title: "Chapter Overview"
	quest.544D302000500001.quest_desc: ["An introduction to Exceptional Power: Reactors in Too Much Magic.", "This chapter's full questline is still being written. This optional overview does not unlock or gate any other chapter."]
	quest.544D508000100000.title: "Tech Overview: Energy Without a Tech Pack"
	quest.544D508000100000.quest_desc: ["Too Much Magic deliberately limits its industrial ecosystem. BiggerReactors Rework provides nuclear generation, its own battery, turbines and processor. Draconic Evolution provides generators, FE routing, the expandable Energy Core bank and later the high-risk Draconic Reactor. There is no Create, AE2 or generic FE transport mod."]
	quest.544D508000200000.title: "Read the Reactor Guide"
	quest.544D508000200000.quest_desc: ["Craft BiggerReactors Rework's Reactor Guide and consult its current build diagrams, calculator and materials pages. This particular 1.21.1 rework has its own machine and fuel behavior; don't blindly follow older Big Reactors measurements."]
	quest.544D508000300000.title: "Prepare Uranium Fuel"
	quest.544D508000300000.quest_desc: ["Obtain two uranium ingots from the allowed deep exploration or mining route, then check the Reactor Guide's fuel handling. The stricter uranium distribution envisioned for this pack is not implemented merely by writing this quest."]
	quest.544D508000400000.title: "Prepare Graphite Moderators"
	quest.544D508000400000.quest_desc: ["Acquire four graphite ingots. Graphite can be used as a reactor moderator and several machine components. The exact build should follow BiggerReactors Rework's in-game Reactor Guide and JEI."]
	quest.544D508000500000.title: "Lay the Reactor Casing"
	quest.544D508000500000.quest_desc: ["Craft at least eight Reactor Casings. Reactor frames require casing edges and corners; some wall/roof faces can use Reactor Glass. The machine must form a closed rectangular shell; verify the valid dimensions in the guide."]
	quest.544D508000600000.title: "Set Up Fuel Rods"
	quest.544D508000600000.quest_desc: ["Craft two Reactor Fuel Rods. Inside the shell, fuel columns must run continuously from floor toward roof. Each column is topped by its own Reactor Control Rod in the roof; no gaps are permitted."]
	quest.544D508000700000.title: "Install a Control Rod"
	quest.544D508000700000.quest_desc: ["Make a Reactor Control Rod for the top of a fuel column. Greater rod insertion reduces reaction rate; start conservatively, then adjust for efficient FE and fuel consumption."]
	quest.544D508000800000.title: "Add the Reactor Terminal"
	quest.544D508000800000.quest_desc: ["Craft the Reactor Terminal and install it in an exterior face. Use its GUI to see assembly errors, temperatures, waste, power output and rod-control state; it is the principal machine panel."]
	quest.544D508000900000.title: "Fit the Fuel Access Port"
	quest.544D508000900000.quest_desc: ["Make an Access Port. Feed uranium fuel and remove cyanite waste through correctly configured ports. Do not confuse the input and output settings, especially when automating."]
	quest.544D508000A00000.title: "Fit the FE Power Tap"
	quest.544D508000A00000.quest_desc: ["Craft a Power Tap and install it on the exterior. Passive reactors export FE through taps; coolant-cooled designs use coolant ports instead and require a different, deliberate setup."]
	quest.544D508000B00000.title: "Assemble and Start a Bigger Reactor"
	quest.544D508000B00000.quest_desc: ["Build a closed casing shell with the terminal, fuel rod columns topped by control rods, fuel access and an FE output. Open the terminal, correct assembly errors, add fuel, connect an energy consumer/bank, then start at low output. Check FE production, heat and fuel usage yourself before marking complete."]
	quest.544D508000C00000.title: "Recover Cyanite Waste"
	quest.544D508000C00000.quest_desc: ["Retrieve cyanite from a running reactor's waste. This is a useful byproduct rather than just a loss; the mod includes an industrial processing pathway."]
	quest.544D508000D00000.title: "Build the Industrial Processor"
	quest.544D508000D00000.quest_desc: ["Craft the Industrial Processor to explore cyanite reprocessing into higher-tier nuclear materials. Check the actual input, water and FE requirements in the machine UI and JEI; do not assume automatic material recycling without connections."]
	quest.544D508000E00000.title: "Build a Battery Shell"
	quest.544D508000E00000.quest_desc: ["Craft eight Battery Casings. Rework's optional rectangular battery uses casing on every frame edge and corner; glass can fill eligible exterior faces. This is a smaller FE storage option distinct from the enormous Draconic Energy Core."]
	quest.544D508000F00000.title: "Install Battery Cells"
	quest.544D508000F00000.quest_desc: ["Obtain four Battery Cells. Place them within the rectangular shell. Cells define stored energy and per-tick input/output throughput, and charged cells retain their energy when moved."]
	quest.544D508001000000.title: "Install the Battery Terminal"
	quest.544D508001000000.quest_desc: ["Craft a Battery Terminal. It displays charge and transfer; the machine needs at least one cell, a terminal, and two Energy Ports to assemble."]
	quest.544D508001100000.title: "Give the Battery Two Ports"
	quest.544D508001100000.quest_desc: ["Craft at least two Battery Energy Ports. Once assembled, configure one as FE input and one as FE output; the wrench and port UI control direction."]
	quest.544D508001200000.title: "Operate the Nuclear Battery"
	quest.544D508001200000.quest_desc: ["Finish the casing/cell/terminal/port structure, link reactor output to battery input and battery output to a consumer. Observe both charge and throughput. This operation is confirmed manually because the quest book has no actual FE telemetry task."]
	quest.544D508001300000.title: "Try a Steam Turbine"
	quest.544D508001300000.quest_desc: ["Optional advanced nuclear branch: the turbine needs a closed casing, two bearings, a continuous shaft, rotor blades, appropriate coils and correctly configured fluid/power ports. Use the Rework guide for accepted coils and fluid loops."]
	quest.544D508001400000.title: "Try a Heat Exchanger"
	quest.544D508001400000.quest_desc: ["Optional infrastructure for coolant/steam loops. Build a valid heat-exchanger structure and connect the flows according to Rework's current guide; it is not needed for a basic passive FE reactor."]
	quest.544D508001500000.title: "Craft a Draconic Generator"
	quest.544D508001500000.quest_desc: ["Draconic Evolution supplies a basic generator for starting its FE network. This path can be explored independently of nuclear generation; JEI confirms the fuel and exact recipe in this installed build."]
	quest.544D508001600000.title: "Craft the Draconic Energy Core"
	quest.544D508001600000.quest_desc: ["Craft the Energy Core block. It is the center of a multiblock FE storage bank, not the unstable power-producing Draconic Reactor Core. Pick a protected site and keep your generation and storage separate."]
	quest.544D508001700000.title: "Prepare Energy Core Stabilizers"
	quest.544D508001700000.quest_desc: ["Craft four Energy Core Stabilizers. Arrange them symmetrically in a single plane outside the desired spherical core shell. Larger storage tiers need additional structural blocks; check the in-game Build Guide for each tier."]
	quest.544D508001800000.title: "Build Input and Output Pylons"
	quest.544D508001800000.quest_desc: ["Craft two Energy Pylons, one for charging and another for discharge. Link them to the Energy Core as the actual FE input/output interface; configure each direction separately in the installed build."]
	quest.544D508001900000.title: "Activate the Draconic Power Bank"
	quest.544D508001900000.quest_desc: ["Assemble the Energy Core and four stabilizers, consult the core's Build Guide and tier controls, activate the completed structure, and configure one pylon as input and another as output. Connect a source and consumer; verify stored FE increases and decreases. Never dismantle a charged core without first checking loss behavior."]
	quest.544D508001A00000.title: "Route FE with a Crystal"
	quest.544D508001A00000.quest_desc: ["Craft a Basic Energy I/O Crystal. Draconic Evolution's crystal networking is the pack's intended FE transfer solution, with relay and wireless variants for more complex layouts. Configure input/output direction before connecting machines."]
	quest.544D508001B00000.title: "Regulate Power with a Flux Gate"
	quest.544D508001B00000.quest_desc: ["Build a Flux Gate for controlled FE throughput. A Draconic Reactor needs controlled power delivery and extraction rather than an unrestricted connection, and its safety should be tested in a disposable world."]
	quest.544D508001C00000.title: "Acquire the Draconic Reactor Core"
	quest.544D508001C00000.quest_desc: ["Craft the Draconic Reactor Core—the high-output, high-risk FE generator. Inspect its *exact installed recipe*: it may require Chaos Shards or other resources that can only be acquired after the Guardian, and this quest does not grant or bypass those materials."]
	quest.544D508001D00000.title: "Four Reactor Stabilizers"
	quest.544D508001D00000.quest_desc: ["Craft four Reactor Stabilizers and arrange them around the Draconic Reactor Core with unobstructed line of sight at the proper spacing for this version. These maintain the containment field; they are *not* Energy Core Stabilizers."]
	quest.544D508001E00000.title: "Build the Reactor Energy Injector"
	quest.544D508001E00000.quest_desc: ["Craft the Reactor Energy Injector and ensure it can continuously supply FE to maintain the containment field during operation. Design independent field-power reserves and a safe shutdown path before attempting a start."]
	quest.544D508001F00000.title: "Plan Safe Reactor Containment"
	quest.544D508001F00000.quest_desc: ["On a disposable world, plan a remote reactor site away from your base and important chunks. Separate high-output extraction from containment-field input, add controlled Flux Gate paths and a sufficient battery buffer. A reactor field collapse or runaway heat can destroy the area; do not treat this as safe baseline generation."]
	quest.544D508002000000.title: "Operate a Draconic Reactor Safely"
	quest.544D508002000000.quest_desc: ["Only after the structure and sufficient fuel are assembled: monitor temperature, containment field strength, fuel conversion and energy saturation. Start with conservative settings, verify field power is sustained under peak load, and test emergency shutdown in an expendable world. This checkmark is a *manual safety acknowledgment*; it does not certify actual reactor telemetry."]
